    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In Riverbend, the boutique sells about eighty‑five percent of its clothes under LaFleur’s own brand.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yvonne_LaFleur"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "LaFleur opened the shop in 1969 as You Boutique, then renamed it in 1984 after launching her signature perfume.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yvonne_LaFleur",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Riverbend’s boutique offers on‑location alterations and bespoke orders, a skill LaFleur honed while working in Paris.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yvonne_LaFleur"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "LaFleur, a skilled milliner, inherited hat blocks from her aunt, adding a distinctive hat collection to the Riverbend shop.",
